# Must PASS: precise nested cite Art. 25(4)(a)(v) resolves (review 7).
# Citation grammar must accept multi-level paths, not force coarsening to "4".

tundra: nested-point-ok-fixture
kind: obligations

regulation:
  id: MIFID_II
  instrument: "Directive 2014/65/EU"
  eli: "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2014/65/oj"
  edition: "OJ L 173, 12.6.2014"

roles:
  - Investment firm
  - Client

contracts:
  - id: structured-deposit-execution-only-class
    text: >
      For execution-only under Art. 25(4), the Investment firm may treat
      structured deposits as in the non-complex class excluding those that
      incorporate a structure which makes it difficult for the Client to
      understand the risk of return or the cost of exiting before term.
    cite:
      - article: "25"
        paragraph: "4(a)(v)"
        quote: "structured deposits, excluding those that incorporate a structure which makes it difficult for the client to understand the risk of return"
    translation_review:
      status: unreviewed

scenarios:
  - name: "Error: complex structured deposit treated as non-complex"
    steps:
      - Given the Investment firm offers execution-only services
      - When a structured deposit embeds a hard-to-understand return structure and is treated as paragraph 4(a)(v) non-complex
      - Then the contract [structured-deposit-execution-only-class] is broken
